.TH GREENLINT 1 "2026-09" "greenlint" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
greenlint \- static linter for carbon-inefficient code and CI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B greenlint
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans source and CI configuration for patterns that waste energy \(em work
repeated that could be cached, polling where an event would do, containers
and jobs larger than the work in them \(em and reports each finding with the
reason it costs power.
.PP
With no paths it scans the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-rules
Print every rule with its energy rationale, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
.B text
for humans,
.B json
for tooling,
.B github
for workflow annotations (default text).
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-findings
Exit 1 when anything is found. This is the CI gate.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Path to the config file.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " GLOB"
Skip paths matching this glob. Repeatable, and added to the config's own
.B ignore
list.
.TP
.BI \-\-baseline " FILE"
Accept the findings recorded in FILE, so that only new ones fail. This is
how an existing codebase adopts the linter without a flag day.
.TP
.BR \-\-write\-baseline " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Record every current finding as accepted, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No findings, or findings without
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-findings .
.TP
.B 1
Findings, with
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-findings .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Scan this repository:
.PP
.RS
.B greenlint
.RE
.PP
Gate a pull request, ignoring what was already there:
.PP
.RS
.B greenlint \-\-baseline .greenlint-baseline.json \-\-fail\-on\-findings
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR carbon-badge (1),
.BR sci (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/greenlint
.UE
